    "result_text": "The build passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customer-code de-duplication in `AssignCustomerCode.java`. This step runs in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline before `SaveOwner`, so the repository holds only existing owners (not the one being created).\n\nThe change:\n- Computes the deterministic base code `<REGION>-<HASH8>` as before.\n- Collects all existing owners' `customerCode` values via `OwnerRepository.findAll()`.\n- If the base code is already taken, appends `-<n>` starting at `n = 2` and increments until the code is unique, then assigns it.\n\nDistinct owners now always receive distinct customer codes. Both the new acceptance test (`coreCustomerCodesStayUnique`) and the full suite pass green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures).",
